---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { classes } from '../../styles';
---
<DocsLayout title="Variants" description="Prefix utilities with screen, state, structure, relationship, attribute, or custom conditions."><header><p class={classes.eyebrow}>Core concept</p><h1 class={classes.title}>Variants</h1><p class={classes.lead}>Prefix utilities with screen, state, structure, relationship, attribute, or custom conditions.</p></header><section class={classes.section}><h2 class={classes.heading}>Stack variants</h2><pre class={classes.code}><code>md:hover:bg-blue-700 dark:text-white before:content-['required']</code></pre></section><section class={classes.section}><h2 class={classes.heading}>Supported forms</h2><p class={classes.copy}>Screen variants include sm through 2xl, max-*, min-[value], and max-[value]. Use dark and print for environment variants. States include hover, focus, disabled, checked, valid, invalid, and child states. Relationship forms include group-*, peer-*, has-*, in-*, not-*, * and **. Attribute forms use data-* and aria-*. Custom selector variants need &amp;. Custom at-rule variants accept @media and @supports.</p></section><section class={classes.section}><h2 class={classes.heading}>Custom-element states</h2><pre class={classes.code}><code>state-[open]:block group-state-[expanded]:text-white peer-state-[selected]:opacity-100</code></pre><p class={classes.copy}>These emit :state(name) on the element, a .group ancestor, or a preceding .peer sibling. Names must be CSS identifiers.</p></section></DocsLayout>
